# 63_non_key_projection_refused
# **Refused, where the column used to be dropped.** `n` is neither grouped nor aggregated, so
# it has one value per row and the result has one row per group: there is no value to report.
# PostgreSQL says `column "t.n" must appear in the GROUP BY clause or be used in an aggregate
# function`; this used to emit the two columns the aggregate operator happened to produce and
# say nothing, so a view's schema was not the schema its author wrote.
REFUSED NL0517
